{"chunk_id": "31c13768c5a9", "text": "Mortally wounded by Rama\u2019s arrow, the mighty monkey king Bali delivers his final words to his brother Sugriva. Recognizing his own past errors and the inevitability of fate, he renounces resentment and accepts Sugriva\u2019s rule over the monkey kingdom. Bali\u2019s chief concern becomes the future: he pleads with Sugriva to protect his son Angada as a father would and to heed the wise counsel of Tara. He also urges loyalty to Rama, warning that disobedience would bring punishment. As a final symbolic act, Bali hands over his golden chain\u2014the sign of royal fortune\u2014to Sugriva. After advising Angada to serve Sugriva faithfully and practice restraint and balance, Bali dies in great pain. His death triggers grief among the monkey hosts, marking a pivotal transfer of power that enables Rama\u2019s alliance with Sugriva.\nMortally wounded, Bali reconciles with Sugriva, entrusts Angada to him, advises loyalty to Rama, and dies after giving away his royal golden chain.\nThemes: deathbed reconciliation, kingship succession, paternal counsel, loyalty to Rama, grief and duty", "vector": [-0.0023648899514228106, -0.029943929985165596, -0.008105278015136719, -0.007744589354842901, 0.0009859378915280104, 0.021695738658308983, -0.03250277414917946, 0.0004329960502218455, -0.022839052602648735, -0.008976373821496964, 0.003184945322573185, 0.009990383870899677, 0.011569245718419552, 0.010888702236115932, -0.011521607637405396, 0.01290311198681593, 0.0503058023750782, 0.0024091252125799656, 0.0319855622947216, -0.010983978398144245, 0.0035048010759055614, 0.006124895066022873, -0.012433536350727081, -0.005951356142759323, -0.0003959914611186832, 0.010201352648437023, 0.0012862279545515776, -0.02268933318555355, 0.00920095294713974, -0.013420325703918934, -0.0008549332269467413, -0.016509994864463806, -0.0024091252125799656, 0.007635702379047871, -0.016033614054322243, -0.001970174489542842, -0.007104878313839436, 0.0044201323762536